<title>SINGAPORE: 3Com to spend S$98 mln on Singapore site.</title>
<headline>3Com to spend S$98 mln on Singapore site.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>3Com Corp, a manufacturer of high volume networking products, said on Tuesday it will invest Singapore $98 million in the first-phase development of a manufacturing site in Singapore.</p>
<p>The new facility, due to open in the first half of 1998, will be 3Com's first production site in the Asia-Pacific region, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>When completed, the facility will contain two production lines, a logistics centre, regional support centre and a regional data centre.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
